Within the context of the heavy quark symmetry, we have used the bag model to calculate the semileptonic decay widths of a doubly charmed baryon. By employing the quark mass values of $m_c=1.35\,{m GeV}$ and $m_b=5.9\,{m GeV}$, we have determined the decay widths of the $B$-type transitions, such as $\Xi_{cc}^{++}	o\Xi_{c}^{++}\ell ar{
u}$ and $\Xi_{bb}	o\Xi_{c}^{++}\ell ar{
u}$. Furthermore, we have also calculated the decay widths of the $D$-type transitions, such as $\Xi_{cc}^{++}	o\Xi_{c}^{0}\ell ar{
u}$ and $\Xi_{cc}^{++}	o\Xi_{b}^{0}\ell ar{
u}$. Our analysis indicates that the decay widths of the $B$-type transitions are approximately $0.1\,{m ps}^{-1}$, while the $D$-type transitions have widths of about $10^{-4}\,{m ps}^{-1}$.
